{"id": "wwdc2019-520", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/520", "wordCount": 3956, "segments": [{"start": 7.0, "text": "I am Michael Diu from the"}, {"start": 8.0, "text": "Interactive Haptics Team."}, {"start": 10.0, "text": "And I am forward to sharing the"}, {"start": 11.0, "text": "many advances in haptics in iOS 13"}, {"start": 13.0, "text": "with you."}, {"start": 15.0, "text": "Let's take a look at our agenda."}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "First, we'll find out where we"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "can use Core Haptics."}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "How it fits in with other audio"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "and haptic APIs."}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "And we'll talk about the two"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "groups of classes in the API."}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "And the basic dimensions and"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "descriptors that we will use to"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "describe our haptics and audio"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "We're going to walk through the"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "basic recipe to start playing"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "out that content."}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "And then we're going to move on"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "to introducing dynamic"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "parameters."}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "And dynamic parameters are a way"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "that you can customize your"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "haptic patterns at playback time"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "in response to your user or your"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "apps behavior."}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "And we're going to explore a new"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "way to express, store, and share"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "your audio haptics content."}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "A new file format we're calling"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "the Apple Haptic Audio Pattern,"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "or AHAP."}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "So let's get to it."}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "First, what is Core Haptics?"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "We can think of it as an"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "event-based audio and haptic"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "rendering API."}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "Or synthesizer for iPhone."}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "We can continue to use our other"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "audio and haptics and feedback"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "API's like AVAudioPlayer and"}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "UIKit's UIFeedbackGenerator in"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "parallel with Core Haptics."}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "You might be wondering, \"Which"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "iPhones can I use this on?\""}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "With one, just one API and one"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "file format, we will be able to"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "access hundreds of millions of"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "haptic engine-equipped iPhones"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "starting from iPhone 8 onward."}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "And we've taken care that your"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "haptic patterns will have the"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "same feel across all of these"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "products."}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "So much so that you're going to"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "be able to prototype and release"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "just using one product."}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "And these iPhones aren't"}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "equipped with just any old"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "commodity actuator."}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "They all have the Apple-designed"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "taptic engine. Which offers you that unique"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "combination of power, a wide,"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "expressive range, and an"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "unmatched precision and control"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "and subtlety."}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "Next, I'd like to talk about"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "those of you who have already"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "started adopting haptics on"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "iPhone with UIKit's"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "feedback-generated API's."}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "Now Core Haptics is not a"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "replacement for this API."}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "In most cases, you want to keep"}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "on using FeedbackGenerator,"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "especially for UIKit controls"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "and adding haptics to that."}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "With that API, you indicate the"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "design intent for your event."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "Whether that's a selection, an"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "impact, or a notification."}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "And you let someone else, Apple,"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "worry about developing a"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "vocabulary to express that and"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "mixing the right modalities like"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "audio haptics animation to"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "communicate that message."}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "Now, this API is also being"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "improved in iOS 13."}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "So please check out its"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "documentation for more details."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "In contrast, Core Haptics is"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "good when you want to be your"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "own sound and haptic designer."}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "With it, you develop your own"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "patterns."}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "And you can have a lot more"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "control over exactly what time"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "it gets played."}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "So you can synchronize with"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "other API's like an animation"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "from Core Animation."}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "Or a sound event from"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "AVAudioEngine."}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "You have a much richer set of"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "playback and modulation"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "controls."}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "Now, UIKit is built on top of"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "Core Haptics."}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "So both API's share the same"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "low-latency performance"}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "characteristics."}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "Now"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "designing your own haptic"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "patterns is going to take more"}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "time."}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "But when it allows you to do"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "something that you couldn't"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "otherwise do and when it allows"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "you to differentiate your app,"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "then it's worth thinking about."}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "Now next, I'd like to talk a bit"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "more about those audio"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "capabilities."}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "So Core Haptics is also an Audio"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "API."}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "And so that allows you to play"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "short, synthesized or custom"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "waveform audio in"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "synchronization, tight sync with"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "your haptics."}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "This type of audio haptic"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "duality has been crucial to many"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "of Apple's own haptics"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "experiences."}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "Like the haptic home button in"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "iPhone 7, the haptic crown in"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "Series 4 Watch, and the"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "UIDatePicker, those scrolling"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "wheels that you use to select"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "dates and times and alarms and"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "calendars."}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "And you may not have realized"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "that. You may not even have noticed"}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "that there was audio in these"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "experiences."}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "But if you were to cover up that"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "audio once you take it away,"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "you'll realize that it's an"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "inseparable an integral part of"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "that experience."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "So now, you can do the same with"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "Core Haptics in your own apps."}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "And I want to talk about some"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "categories of apps, one app -- a"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "huge category in particular"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "where you might want to think"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "about Core Haptics, and that's"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "games."}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "So imagine we are at the race"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "track."}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "We want to go into turbo mode."}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "Let's imagine."}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "When you've got that brute force"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "message to deliver, think about"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "using synchronized haptics and"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "audio in your app to generate"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "those visceral explosions and"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "rumbles."}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "Now another very nice"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "application is for to simulate"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "physical contact to make your"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "applications feel more"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "realistic."}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "Think about a tennis game."}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "You could have audio and haptic"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "components where the pitch of"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "your audio, the intensity of"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "your haptics are proportional to"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "how fast your swing is or how"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "centered the ball lands in the"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "middle of the racket."}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "And you can even control how"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "long the strings your racket"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "will resonate for after the"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "impact."}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "So another great area to think"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "about using Core Haptics is in"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "augmented reality apps."}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "And there, if you're working in"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "this space, you're already"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "familiar with the benefits of"}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "having high visual fidelity"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "paired with 3D audio working in"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "concert. Now we can reach for that next"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "level of immersion by"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "considering how custom haptic"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "feedback can ground our user"}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "gestures,"}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "or respond to app, device, and"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "AR object events."}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "For example, moving your device"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "around or moving your entire"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "users around."}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "As an inspiration this year,"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "we've enhanced the Swift Shot"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "sample code by using haptics"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "that are modulated based on how"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "fast you pull back the sling."}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "How fast you pull back your"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "phone. You're going to feel the tension"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "building up as you stretch it"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "back. And then a very satisfying thunk"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "as you release."}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "I'd like to show you a video of"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "this and I'm going to use audio"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "to represent just the haptics"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "that you're going to feel."}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "They're going to sound like"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "this."}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "Now, we're going to see the"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "whole thing together."}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "Visuals and haptics, no regular"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "audio."}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "So that was an example of how we"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "can use haptics, sound, and"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "visuals all synchronized"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "together to enhance our AR"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "Now these are just a few"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "categories of apps, games, and"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "AR that are ripe for creative"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "explorations, with haptics and"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "the corresponding sounds."}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "I'm sure you're going to think"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "of many, many more."}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "So now let's get into how we can"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "start expressing our content"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "with Core Haptics."}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "There are just two groups of"}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "classes in Core Haptics."}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "There's those to represent your"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "And those to playback that"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 524.0, "text": "Let's take a closer look at the"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "content side first."}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "The basic indivisible content"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "elements is in Core Haptics is"}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "called a CHHapticEvent."}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "Now, each event has a type and a"}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "time. And optionally, parameters that"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "will customize its feel."}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "These events can overlap each"}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "other and when they do, they"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "mix."}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "And all events are grouped into"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "a pattern."}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "Next, I'd like to talk about"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "those types of events that we"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "can have."}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "Our first type is called the"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "HapticTransient."}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "The HapticTransient, I think of"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "it as a gavel."}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "It's a striking motion."}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "It's momentary and"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "instantaneous."}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "And then we have two continuous"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "types."}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "We have HapticContinuous and"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "AudioContinuous."}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "And there I think of, for"}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "example, bowing a stringed"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "instrument."}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "It is longer than a transient."}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "It can be, for example, used as"}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "a background texture."}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "And you have a much richer set"}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "of knobs that you can use."}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "For example, to modulate the"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "resonance of it."}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "Lastly, we have the AudioCustom"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "type. And the AudioCustom, as we -- as"}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "I mentioned earlier."}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "Is where you can provide your"}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "own audio to be played back in"}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "sync with the haptics."}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "Next, let's talk about some of"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "those optional parameters."}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "Our first event parameter is"}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "called HapticIntesnity."}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "And it has an audio analog,"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "audio volume, which you're"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "probably already familiar with."}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "Now, with this parameter, you go"}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "from no output as you turn, and"}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "as you turn the knob from zero"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "all the way up to one, you go to"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "the maximum output of the"}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "system."}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "Our next parameter is called"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "HapticSharpness."}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "Now HapticSharpness is a new"}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "concept. There's no physical analog to"}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "this and there's also no audio"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "analog."}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "In this world, I want you to"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "instead think of moving along in"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "a perceptual space from a very"}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "round and organic feel at zero,"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "all the way to a more crisp and"}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "precise feel at one."}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "And to help ground that a bit"}, {"start": 672.0, "text": "further, I'm going to use some"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "examples from iOS 12."}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "The flashlight button on your"}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "lock screen is an example of a"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "very high sharpness haptic."}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "And the App Switcher, that swipe"}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "up, that's an example of a more"}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "round, a lower sharpness haptic."}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "As for the why."}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "Why were those two types of"}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "experiences, you know, sharp and"}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "not sharp? I'm going to refer you to our"}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "talk on Audio Haptic Design."}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "Now, we have several more types"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "of event parameters, for"}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "example, that apply to audio,"}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "like pitch and pan."}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "And for haptics, we have things"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "that let you change those"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "resonance and so forth."}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "But these two, intensity and"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "sharpness, will be enough to get"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "us going."}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "Now, to develop a feel for that"}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "dynamic range and precision of"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "intensity and sharpness."}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "We've got a sample code, the"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "palette, which allows you to try"}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "out these experiences for"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "yourself."}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "As you move, as you tap, or you"}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "drag your finger around, you'll"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "be accessing the sharpness axis,"}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "as well as the intensity axis."}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "And it's going to play out the"}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "corresponding continuous or"}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "transient haptic as you do that."}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "This will help you get that"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "intuition."}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "So that was an introduction"}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "about where we can use Core"}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "Haptics and also how to specify"}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "our content."}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "Now, let's invite Doug Scott,"}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "our Core Haptics architect, to"}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "get us started with playing back"}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "Core Haptics, playing back those"}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "patterns, and integrating Core"}, {"start": 784.0, "text": "Haptics into our apps."}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "Please welcome Doug."}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "Thank you, Michael."}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "Good evening, everyone."}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "I am thrilled to be here to talk"}, {"start": 796.0, "text": "to you about integrating the"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "Core Haptics API into your"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "applications."}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "Before I show a demo and dive"}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "into the code, let's walk"}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "through the basic steps that"}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "your application will follow"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "when you want to play a haptic pattern."}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "Creating your content is the"}, {"start": 814.0, "text": "first good step because this can"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "be done at any point prior to"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "the point where you need to use"}, {"start": 819.0, "text": "it."}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "In this example, we load an"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "NSDictionary into a haptic"}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "pattern."}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "The dictionary might have been"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "something that we stored in our"}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "application as part of our"}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "resources."}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "As we will see later, patterns"}, {"start": 832.0, "text": "can also be created right before"}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "they are to be played if they"}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "need to very interactively in"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "response to changes in your"}, {"start": 838.0, "text": "application."}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "The next step is to create an"}, {"start": 843.0, "text": "instance of the haptic engine."}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "This should be done as soon as"}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "your application knows that it"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "will be making use of haptics."}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "Next, you create a haptic player"}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "for your haptic pattern."}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "Each player is associated with a"}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "single pattern and a particular"}, {"start": 859.0, "text": "haptic engine."}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "Starting the haptic engine tells"}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "the system to initialize the"}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "audio and haptic hardware in"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "preparation for request to play"}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "the pattern."}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "At the moment that your"}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "application wants the pattern to"}, {"start": 876.0, "text": "play. You start the player."}, {"start": 878.0, "text": "This can be done in two modes."}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "The first is called -- which we"}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "call immediate mode tells the"}, {"start": 884.0, "text": "system that you wish this"}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "pattern to play at the soonest"}, {"start": 887.0, "text": "possible moment with the minimal"}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "latency."}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "The second, in scheduled mode,"}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "you hand it an absolute"}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "timestamp which tells the system"}, {"start": 896.0, "text": "that you want to synchronize"}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "this event with some other"}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "systems such as another audio"}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "player or a game event or a"}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "graphics event."}, {"start": 908.0, "text": "If you want to know when your"}, {"start": 909.0, "text": "pattern is finished playing, you"}, {"start": 911.0, "text": "can have the haptic engine"}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "notify you via callback when"}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "your player or players are done."}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "Here, the engine calls back to"}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "the application."}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "And the application can now"}, {"start": 922.0, "text": "choose to stop the haptic engine"}, {"start": 924.0, "text": "or continue on with the next"}, {"start": 926.0, "text": "haptic pattern."}, {"start": 929.0, "text": "Those are the basic steps."}, {"start": 930.0, "text": "Now let's see an example of an"}, {"start": 932.0, "text": "application which uses this"}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "system."}, {"start": 936.0, "text": "But before we do, we need to let"}, {"start": 938.0, "text": "you in on a secret demonstrating"}, {"start": 941.0, "text": "the use of an API which"}, {"start": 942.0, "text": "generates tactile feedback"}, {"start": 944.0, "text": "prevents -- presents a unique"}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "problem."}, {"start": 947.0, "text": "You in the audience can't feel"}, {"start": 948.0, "text": "it."}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "The way we handle this was by"}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "adding an audio equivalent for"}, {"start": 952.0, "text": "each haptic event into the"}, {"start": 953.0, "text": "output which will let you hear"}, {"start": 955.0, "text": "the effect of the haptics."}, {"start": 960.0, "text": "This application uses a simple"}, {"start": 962.0, "text": "physics engine to move the ball"}, {"start": 964.0, "text": "around the screen in response to"}, {"start": 965.0, "text": "the accelerometer."}, {"start": 969.0, "text": "It generates haptic and audio"}, {"start": 970.0, "text": "feedback when the ball impacts"}, {"start": 972.0, "text": "the edges of the screen."}, {"start": 974.0, "text": "The user has the sense they are"}, {"start": 975.0, "text": "feeling the impacts through the"}, {"start": 976.0, "text": "edges of the game wall as well"}, {"start": 978.0, "text": "as hearing them."}, {"start": 979.0, "text": "The harder the ball hits the"}, {"start": 980.0, "text": "edge, the more intense the"}, {"start": 981.0, "text": "haptic and the louder the audio."}, {"start": 986.0, "text": "Okay, let's look at the code for"}, {"start": 988.0, "text": "this example to see how to"}, {"start": 989.0, "text": "integrate the Core Haptics API"}, {"start": 991.0, "text": "into your application."}, {"start": 992.0, "text": "We'll see how event parameters"}, {"start": 994.0, "text": "are used to produce changes in"}, {"start": 996.0, "text": "the haptics and audio."}, {"start": 998.0, "text": "The example here, all this code,"}, {"start": 1000.0, "text": "is taken from the sample code on"}, {"start": 1002.0, "text": "the website."}, {"start": 1003.0, "text": "But it's been edited down to"}, {"start": 1004.0, "text": "show the important points."}, {"start": 1008.0, "text": "First, we import the Core"}, {"start": 1010.0, "text": "Haptics module. Along with the other modules we"}, {"start": 1012.0, "text": "need for the application."}, {"start": 1017.0, "text": "The CHHapticEngine is declared"}, {"start": 1019.0, "text": "as a member variable of our"}, {"start": 1020.0, "text": "ViewController because we want"}, {"start": 1021.0, "text": "to be able to control its"}, {"start": 1022.0, "text": "lifetime and have it exist for"}, {"start": 1024.0, "text": "the lifetime of the application."}, {"start": 1028.0, "text": "As discussed in our flow chart"}, {"start": 1029.0, "text": "earlier, we set up the haptic"}, {"start": 1031.0, "text": "engine in advance of when we"}, {"start": 1032.0, "text": "want to use it."}, {"start": 1033.0, "text": "Here, we call a helper method at"}, {"start": 1035.0, "text": "the point that the view has"}, {"start": 1037.0, "text": "loaded."}, {"start": 1040.0, "text": "In the helper method, we began"}, {"start": 1041.0, "text": "by creating the instance of the"}, {"start": 1043.0, "text": "haptic engine and check for"}, {"start": 1045.0, "text": "possible errors."}, {"start": 1046.0, "text": "The engine is assigned to our"}, {"start": 1048.0, "text": "member variable so we can keep"}, {"start": 1049.0, "text": "it around."}, {"start": 1052.0, "text": "It is optional, but extremely"}, {"start": 1054.0, "text": "useful to assign a closure to"}, {"start": 1056.0, "text": "the engine's stoppedHandler"}, {"start": 1058.0, "text": "property."}, {"start": 1059.0, "text": "This will be called if the"}, {"start": 1060.0, "text": "engine is stopped by some action"}, {"start": 1062.0, "text": "other than the application"}, {"start": 1064.0, "text": "itself asking it to."}, {"start": 1065.0, "text": "Some possible reasons that this"}, {"start": 1067.0, "text": "might happen are an audio"}, {"start": 1068.0, "text": "session interruption or the"}, {"start": 1070.0, "text": "application being suspended."}, {"start": 1074.0, "text": "We finish this method by"}, {"start": 1075.0, "text": "starting the haptic engine and"}, {"start": 1077.0, "text": "checking for possible errors."}, {"start": 1079.0, "text": "The engine will continue to run"}, {"start": 1080.0, "text": "until the application, or a"}, {"start": 1082.0, "text": "possible outside action stops"}, {"start": 1084.0, "text": "it."}, {"start": 1085.0, "text": "Note that the application tracks"}, {"start": 1087.0, "text": "whether or not the engine needs"}, {"start": 1089.0, "text": "to be restarted."}, {"start": 1091.0, "text": "Typically, you might leave the"}, {"start": 1092.0, "text": "engine running for the entire"}, {"start": 1094.0, "text": "time that you have any view"}, {"start": 1096.0, "text": "visible on the screen which has"}, {"start": 1098.0, "text": "haptic interaction."}, {"start": 1104.0, "text": "Here's the location in the"}, {"start": 1105.0, "text": "application where the simple"}, {"start": 1106.0, "text": "physics engine lets us know that"}, {"start": 1108.0, "text": "the ball has collided with the"}, {"start": 1109.0, "text": "wall."}, {"start": 1110.0, "text": "In this example, we want to"}, {"start": 1112.0, "text": "generate our haptic and audio"}, {"start": 1113.0, "text": "pattern to interactively track"}, {"start": 1115.0, "text": "the velocity of the ball."}, {"start": 1117.0, "text": "So the pattern player and its"}, {"start": 1118.0, "text": "pattern are created at the"}, {"start": 1120.0, "text": "moment they are needed."}, {"start": 1124.0, "text": "This method is responsible for"}, {"start": 1125.0, "text": "creating the pattern to be"}, {"start": 1126.0, "text": "played in response to the ball"}, {"start": 1128.0, "text": "collision."}, {"start": 1129.0, "text": "In here, we will create a"}, {"start": 1130.0, "text": "pattern with two events."}, {"start": 1132.0, "text": "One haptic and one audio."}, {"start": 1136.0, "text": "We create a haptic event of type"}, {"start": 1138.0, "text": "hapticTransient to produce that"}, {"start": 1140.0, "text": "impactful feel."}, {"start": 1144.0, "text": "And we give it two event"}, {"start": 1145.0, "text": "parameters which configure the"}, {"start": 1146.0, "text": "event's sharpness and intensity,"}, {"start": 1148.0, "text": "which you've heard about"}, {"start": 1149.0, "text": "already, based upon the velocity"}, {"start": 1151.0, "text": "of the ball."}, {"start": 1155.0, "text": "Then, we create the audio event"}, {"start": 1157.0, "text": "with type audioContinuous with a"}, {"start": 1160.0, "text": "set of event parameters for"}, {"start": 1162.0, "text": "volume and envelope decay also"}, {"start": 1164.0, "text": "calculated from the ball's"}, {"start": 1166.0, "text": "velocity."}, {"start": 1167.0, "text": "The sustained parameter here"}, {"start": 1169.0, "text": "assures us that the intensity of"}, {"start": 1171.0, "text": "this event will die off to zero"}, {"start": 1173.0, "text": "instead of continuing on for the"}, {"start": 1176.0, "text": "length of the event."}, {"start": 1179.0, "text": "We create a pattern containing"}, {"start": 1181.0, "text": "these two events synchronized in"}, {"start": 1183.0, "text": "time."}, {"start": 1186.0, "text": "Finally, we create the pattern"}, {"start": 1187.0, "text": "player from this pattern and"}, {"start": 1189.0, "text": "return it to this layer, back in"}, {"start": 1192.0, "text": "the method that responds to the"}, {"start": 1193.0, "text": "collision."}, {"start": 1195.0, "text": "The final step is to start the"}, {"start": 1197.0, "text": "pattern player at time"}, {"start": 1198.0, "text": "CHHapticTimeImmediate, which"}, {"start": 1201.0, "text": "indicates to play it back as"}, {"start": 1203.0, "text": "soon as possible with minimal"}, {"start": 1204.0, "text": "latency."}, {"start": 1207.0, "text": "Notice that the app does not"}, {"start": 1208.0, "text": "hold on to the instance of this"}, {"start": 1209.0, "text": "player."}, {"start": 1211.0, "text": "Its pattern is guaranteed to"}, {"start": 1212.0, "text": "continue playing until it is"}, {"start": 1214.0, "text": "finished."}, {"start": 1215.0, "text": "So the application can simply"}, {"start": 1216.0, "text": "fire and forget it."}, {"start": 1220.0, "text": "And that's the basic recipe for"}, {"start": 1222.0, "text": "playing your content using a"}, {"start": 1223.0, "text": "pattern that is created"}, {"start": 1224.0, "text": "programmatically within your"}, {"start": 1225.0, "text": "app's code."}, {"start": 1227.0, "text": "Again, because this app is"}, {"start": 1228.0, "text": "continuously interactive we"}, {"start": 1230.0, "text": "don't stop the haptic engine"}, {"start": 1232.0, "text": "until the game screen is no"}, {"start": 1234.0, "text": "longer visible."}, {"start": 1238.0, "text": "Now let's take a moment to talk"}, {"start": 1239.0, "text": "about one of the most powerful"}, {"start": 1240.0, "text": "capabilities of Core Haptics,"}, {"start": 1242.0, "text": "dynamic parameters."}, {"start": 1246.0, "text": "Dynamic parameters let you"}, {"start": 1248.0, "text": "increase and decrease the value"}, {"start": 1250.0, "text": "of the existing event parameters"}, {"start": 1252.0, "text": "for all active and upcoming"}, {"start": 1254.0, "text": "events in a pattern as it plays."}, {"start": 1258.0, "text": "Dynamic parameters take effect"}, {"start": 1260.0, "text": "at the timestamp you provide."}, {"start": 1262.0, "text": "You can adjust multiple"}, {"start": 1263.0, "text": "different parameters at the same"}, {"start": 1265.0, "text": "time or with any arbitrary time"}, {"start": 1268.0, "text": "relationship."}, {"start": 1271.0, "text": "You can include dynamic"}, {"start": 1272.0, "text": "parameters when you create your"}, {"start": 1273.0, "text": "pattern."}, {"start": 1274.0, "text": "or send them to your player in"}, {"start": 1276.0, "text": "real time during playback."}, {"start": 1280.0, "text": "This allows you to use a single"}, {"start": 1281.0, "text": "pattern to generate an infinite"}, {"start": 1283.0, "text": "number of haptic and audio"}, {"start": 1286.0, "text": "variations by adjusting the"}, {"start": 1288.0, "text": "pattern dynamically."}, {"start": 1292.0, "text": "Let's take a look at an example."}, {"start": 1294.0, "text": "In this diagram, on the bottom,"}, {"start": 1295.0, "text": "we have a haptic pattern that"}, {"start": 1296.0, "text": "was designed with all haptic"}, {"start": 1299.0, "text": "event intensities set to their"}, {"start": 1300.0, "text": "maximum value."}, {"start": 1302.0, "text": "The first half are"}, {"start": 1303.0, "text": "HapticTransients."}, {"start": 1304.0, "text": "The second half is the"}, {"start": 1305.0, "text": "HapticContinuous."}, {"start": 1307.0, "text": "We'd like to reduce the"}, {"start": 1308.0, "text": "intensity of all the games"}, {"start": 1310.0, "text": "haptics temporarily."}, {"start": 1311.0, "text": "For example, if a game -- if a"}, {"start": 1313.0, "text": "character was speaking in the"}, {"start": 1314.0, "text": "game."}, {"start": 1318.0, "text": "I send a dynamic parameter for"}, {"start": 1319.0, "text": "intensity with a value of 0.3"}, {"start": 1322.0, "text": "that takes effect at time .5"}, {"start": 1324.0, "text": "seconds."}, {"start": 1325.0, "text": "You can see that it reduced the"}, {"start": 1327.0, "text": "intensity of the event at that"}, {"start": 1328.0, "text": "time significantly to about a"}, {"start": 1330.0, "text": "third of what it was unmodified."}, {"start": 1336.0, "text": "Finally, let's look at another"}, {"start": 1338.0, "text": "way to create patterns."}, {"start": 1342.0, "text": "So what exactly is AHAP?"}, {"start": 1347.0, "text": "The Apple Haptic Audio Pattern"}, {"start": 1350.0, "text": "is a specification for"}, {"start": 1351.0, "text": "describing a Core Haptics"}, {"start": 1353.0, "text": "pattern in a text-based format."}, {"start": 1356.0, "text": "It is built from nested key"}, {"start": 1357.0, "text": "value pairs which become quite"}, {"start": 1360.0, "text": "familiar for you, to you once"}, {"start": 1362.0, "text": "you start working with the"}, {"start": 1363.0, "text": "classes which make up the Core"}, {"start": 1365.0, "text": "Haptics API."}, {"start": 1368.0, "text": "It is a schema for the widely"}, {"start": 1369.0, "text": "established JSON file format."}, {"start": 1372.0, "text": "Which means you have already"}, {"start": 1375.0, "text": "quite a number of different"}, {"start": 1376.0, "text": "frameworks which can read,"}, {"start": 1377.0, "text": "write, and edit these, including"}, {"start": 1379.0, "text": "such things as the Swift Codable"}, {"start": 1381.0, "text": "framework."}, {"start": 1384.0, "text": "AHAP makes it easy to share and"}, {"start": 1386.0, "text": "edit haptic patterns because it"}, {"start": 1388.0, "text": "is a format that all developers"}, {"start": 1390.0, "text": "can agree on."}, {"start": 1394.0, "text": "Loading your haptic patterns"}, {"start": 1395.0, "text": "from external AHAP files allows"}, {"start": 1397.0, "text": "you to separate your content"}, {"start": 1398.0, "text": "from your application code."}, {"start": 1404.0, "text": "Using the magic of a slide deck,"}, {"start": 1406.0, "text": "we're going to create a simple"}, {"start": 1407.0, "text": "AHAP file here."}, {"start": 1410.0, "text": "We start with a version string."}, {"start": 1413.0, "text": "Which indicates which version of"}, {"start": 1414.0, "text": "the system this pattern was"}, {"start": 1416.0, "text": "designed for."}, {"start": 1419.0, "text": "Next, we add the key for our"}, {"start": 1420.0, "text": "pattern."}, {"start": 1421.0, "text": "Which will be an array of"}, {"start": 1422.0, "text": "dictionaries."}, {"start": 1426.0, "text": "We add our first event"}, {"start": 1427.0, "text": "dictionary to our pattern array."}, {"start": 1429.0, "text": "This event has two required key"}, {"start": 1431.0, "text": "value pairs."}, {"start": 1433.0, "text": "A time in seconds at which the"}, {"start": 1434.0, "text": "event should happen relative to"}, {"start": 1437.0, "text": "the start of the pattern and the"}, {"start": 1438.0, "text": "type of event."}, {"start": 1440.0, "text": "This is a haptic transient event"}, {"start": 1441.0, "text": "starting as soon as the pattern"}, {"start": 1443.0, "text": "starts."}, {"start": 1446.0, "text": "To this event, we add event"}, {"start": 1448.0, "text": "parameters which will affect"}, {"start": 1449.0, "text": "only this event."}, {"start": 1451.0, "text": "These are stored in their own"}, {"start": 1452.0, "text": "array of dictionaries."}, {"start": 1455.0, "text": "We add an event parameter to"}, {"start": 1456.0, "text": "control the intensity of the"}, {"start": 1458.0, "text": "event and another to control its"}, {"start": 1459.0, "text": "sharpness."}, {"start": 1464.0, "text": "We can add a second event in the"}, {"start": 1465.0, "text": "same fashion."}, {"start": 1466.0, "text": "This one starts at an offset of"}, {"start": 1468.0, "text": ".5 seconds from the first and is"}, {"start": 1470.0, "text": "of type HapticContinuous."}, {"start": 1472.0, "text": "For the event parameters, we use"}, {"start": 1474.0, "text": "the same as we had for the first"}, {"start": 1476.0, "text": "event."}, {"start": 1478.0, "text": "Events type HapticContinuous and"}, {"start": 1481.0, "text": "AudioContinuous require an event"}, {"start": 1483.0, "text": "duration in addition to the time"}, {"start": 1485.0, "text": "and event type."}, {"start": 1486.0, "text": "This duration value is always"}, {"start": 1488.0, "text": "specified in seconds."}, {"start": 1492.0, "text": "Here is a visual representation"}, {"start": 1494.0, "text": "of the pattern we just created."}, {"start": 1496.0, "text": "You can see the two types of"}, {"start": 1497.0, "text": "events; the HapticTransient at"}, {"start": 1500.0, "text": "the very beginning, the"}, {"start": 1502.0, "text": "Continuous later with a relative"}, {"start": 1504.0, "text": "timing and duration and their"}, {"start": 1505.0, "text": "intensity and sharpness"}, {"start": 1507.0, "text": "parameter values."}, {"start": 1510.0, "text": "That was a quick tour of AHAP."}, {"start": 1513.0, "text": "This diagram shows a summary of"}, {"start": 1515.0, "text": "the AHAP file structure."}, {"start": 1517.0, "text": "A single pattern consisting of"}, {"start": 1518.0, "text": "an array of event dictionaries,"}, {"start": 1521.0, "text": "optional dynamic parameters, and"}, {"start": 1524.0, "text": "optional use of parameter curves"}, {"start": 1526.0, "text": "which are an extension of"}, {"start": 1528.0, "text": "dynamic parameters."}, {"start": 1529.0, "text": "Which you can read about more"}, {"start": 1531.0, "text": "on, within the information that"}, {"start": 1532.0, "text": "we have on the website."}, {"start": 1535.0, "text": "You can find a full link to the"}, {"start": 1536.0, "text": "AHAP specification on our"}, {"start": 1538.0, "text": "sessions page."}, {"start": 1542.0, "text": "Also on our sessions page,"}, {"start": 1544.0, "text": "you'll find a code example that"}, {"start": 1545.0, "text": "shows how to create, load, and"}, {"start": 1547.0, "text": "play the patterns described by"}, {"start": 1549.0, "text": "AHAP files."}, {"start": 1550.0, "text": "This haptic sampler app includes"}, {"start": 1552.0, "text": "a range of patterns that"}, {"start": 1553.0, "text": "highlight the subtlety, dynamic"}, {"start": 1555.0, "text": "range, and audio haptic sync."}, {"start": 1557.0, "text": "That's possible with the Core"}, {"start": 1559.0, "text": "Haptics API."}, {"start": 1561.0, "text": "Thank you very much."}, {"start": 1562.0, "text": "And now, I'd like to return the"}, {"start": 1563.0, "text": "stage to my colleague, Michael."}, {"start": 1572.0, "text": "Thanks, Doug."}, {"start": 1574.0, "text": "So although we covered a lot of"}, {"start": 1576.0, "text": "ground today there is still much"}, {"start": 1578.0, "text": "more to discover with Core"}, {"start": 1580.0, "text": "Haptics."}, {"start": 1582.0, "text": "Check out the online doc"}, {"start": 1583.0, "text": "reference for details."}, {"start": 1586.0, "text": "Once you're up and running with"}, {"start": 1587.0, "text": "the basics of specifying"}, {"start": 1588.0, "text": "contents and playing that"}, {"start": 1590.0, "text": "content you'll probably be"}, {"start": 1591.0, "text": "wondering about the design"}, {"start": 1593.0, "text": "principles for these joints"}, {"start": 1595.0, "text": "haptic audio patterns."}, {"start": 1598.0, "text": "You'll be wondering do the"}, {"start": 1599.0, "text": "rules, the guidelines for sound"}, {"start": 1601.0, "text": "design carry over to haptic"}, {"start": 1603.0, "text": "design?"}, {"start": 1604.0, "text": "What are some common pitfalls I"}, {"start": 1605.0, "text": "should be aware of?"}, {"start": 1607.0, "text": "The good news is that our Audio"}, {"start": 1610.0, "text": "and Haptic Design teams have"}, {"start": 1612.0, "text": "been doing this for years and"}, {"start": 1613.0, "text": "they've helped put together some"}, {"start": 1615.0, "text": "advice and guidance in an"}, {"start": 1616.0, "text": "updated human interface"}, {"start": 1618.0, "text": "guidelines or HIG for haptics."}, {"start": 1620.0, "text": "As well as in the accompanying"}, {"start": 1622.0, "text": "talk in WWDC this year."}, {"start": 1625.0, "text": "Check it out."}, {"start": 1628.0, "text": "So let's recap."}, {"start": 1630.0, "text": "Today, we talked about where"}, {"start": 1631.0, "text": "haptics can help you reach for"}, {"start": 1633.0, "text": "that next level of immersion and"}, {"start": 1635.0, "text": "make your app interactions more"}, {"start": 1637.0, "text": "effortless."}, {"start": 1639.0, "text": "Having synchronized and"}, {"start": 1640.0, "text": "complimentary audio and haptics"}, {"start": 1643.0, "text": "together is a particularly"}, {"start": 1645.0, "text": "effective combination."}, {"start": 1647.0, "text": "But there haven't been API's"}, {"start": 1649.0, "text": "that allowed you to actually do"}, {"start": 1650.0, "text": "this."}, {"start": 1652.0, "text": "With iOS 13, we now have the"}, {"start": 1654.0, "text": "necessary ingredients to create"}, {"start": 1656.0, "text": "these rich multimodal"}, {"start": 1658.0, "text": "experiences."}, {"start": 1659.0, "text": "We have the vocabulary to"}, {"start": 1661.0, "text": "describe haptics and audio"}, {"start": 1663.0, "text": "events and a file format, AHAP."}, {"start": 1667.0, "text": "We've got a new performant API"}, {"start": 1670.0, "text": "Core Haptics which is designed"}, {"start": 1672.0, "text": "for low latency and real-time"}, {"start": 1674.0, "text": "modulation."}, {"start": 1675.0, "text": "We've put together sample code,"}, {"start": 1679.0, "text": "sample patterns, design"}, {"start": 1681.0, "text": "guidelines, and support from"}, {"start": 1684.0, "text": "Apple. And lastly, you've got an"}, {"start": 1686.0, "text": "incredible audience, incredible"}, {"start": 1688.0, "text": "hardware where you can feel your"}, {"start": 1690.0, "text": "haptics as you intended."}, {"start": 1691.0, "text": "A huge installed base of taptic"}, {"start": 1694.0, "text": "engines that give you the most"}, {"start": 1696.0, "text": "powerful, expressive, and"}, {"start": 1699.0, "text": "precise haptics hardware"}, {"start": 1700.0, "text": "available."}, {"start": 1701.0, "text": "So please come on down to the"}, {"start": 1704.0, "text": "labs on Thursday and Friday"}, {"start": 1706.0, "text": "where you can check out some of"}, {"start": 1708.0, "text": "these haptics samples that we"}, {"start": 1710.0, "text": "showed today and discuss your"}, {"start": 1712.0, "text": "own ideas for your apps."}, {"start": 1714.0, "text": "You'll also find all of these"}, {"start": 1717.0, "text": "guidelines and references online"}, {"start": 1719.0, "text": "at our sessions page."}, {"start": 1722.0, "text": "I know you're going to have a"}, {"start": 1723.0, "text": "lot of fun creating and using"}, {"start": 1726.0, "text": "these haptic patterns in your"}, {"start": 1727.0, "text": "apps."}, {"start": 1728.0, "text": "We can't wait to hear and feel"}, {"start": 1729.0, "text": "what you come up with."}]}